+Translation markers
+-------------------
+
+Load ``jinja2.ext.extractor`` to collect translation messages with
+compile-time metadata. Marker bodies remain ordinary Jinja code::
+
+    {% extract note="Button", priority=2 %}
+        {{ gettext("Open") }}
+    {% endextract %}
+
+``env.extract_marked_translations(source, source_name=None)`` accepts
+text or a parsed template. It yields fresh mappings with ``source``,
+marker ``lineno``, copied ``metadata`` and a ``messages`` list. Message
+entries retain the normal gettext function, line and extracted value.
+Nested calls belong to the enclosing marker. Mutating a returned mapping
+does not change later extraction; compilation retains no marker list.
+Nonconstant metadata and duplicate keys fail with the offending key.
+
+``env.extract_marked_translations_from_templates(names=None)`` extracts
+source from the configured loader without rendering or following
+dependencies. Explicit names follow iterable order; omitted names use
+``env.list_templates()``. Sources identify logical names, not filenames.
+Loaders may return no filename or reload callback. Missing names raise
+``TemplateNotFound``; loaders without listing support require explicit
+names. Normal extraction and Babel comments remain independent.
+
 .. _i18n-extension:
 
 i18n Extension
